1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
A quick tour of the app.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,750
Fishamongus! is a fishing log that lives on your phone. No account, nothing uploaded.

3
00:00:08,750 --> 00:00:13,000
New here? Load a month of sample fishing to look around, and clear it in one tap.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,750
The Now screen shows the weather, wind, pressure trend, tide, moon and water temperature where you stand.

5
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:22,250
Solunar bite times are worked out on the phone from the moon, with a rating for the day.

6
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:27,000
It suggests the lures that have caught you the most fish in conditions like these.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,750
Tap Start fishing when your line goes in. The app times the session and tracks your lure.

8
00:00:31,750 --> 00:00:36,000
Switch lures with one tap, so Stats can show fish per hour for each one.

9
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,750
Tap + to log a catch. Add a photo, then search more than 240 fish by name.

10
00:00:40,750 --> 00:00:45,250
Species with subspecies get a second menu – Florida bass, Westslope cutthroat and more.

11
00:00:45,250 --> 00:00:49,750
Your lure is already on the form, and GPS, weather and tide are filled in automatically.

12
00:00:49,750 --> 00:00:54,500
No scale? Enter the length and the app estimates a typical weight for that fish.

13
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:58,750
Every catch is saved with its photo, lure, place and conditions, grouped by day.

14
00:00:58,750 --> 00:01:02,750
Swipe a catch to edit it, log the same again, or delete it.

15
00:01:02,750 --> 00:01:07,500
Open a catch to see everything. Sections fold away and still show their key values.

16
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:12,750
Stats sums up your log in plain words, always with the number of fish behind it.

17
00:01:12,750 --> 00:01:17,250
See which lures work in each sky, pressure, wind, tide, moon and solunar period.

18
00:01:17,250 --> 00:01:22,000
Timed sessions give fish per hour for each lure – a fairer test than raw counts.

19
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:26,750
Save your spots. Catches made there are linked automatically, and colours show where fish came lately.

20
00:01:26,750 --> 00:01:31,500
Each spot has its own stats: best lures, best conditions and recent catches.

21
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:36,250
Plan a trip: the hourly forecast, with your best hours marked from your own history.

22
00:01:36,250 --> 00:01:41,000
Trip plans add NOAA tides, sunrise and sunset, and the bite times during your trip.

23
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,750
Tap Shellfish to log crab, shrimp, clams, oysters and more. Freshwater and Saltwater shorten the list.

24
00:01:45,750 --> 00:01:50,250
Record sex, shell and width, plus pots and soak time. A crab you can’t keep gets a warning before you save it.

25
00:01:50,250 --> 00:01:54,750
One tap adds the WDFW crab, clam and oyster limits. Clams count together toward the 40-clam limit.

26
00:01:54,750 --> 00:01:59,250
Stats shows what each pot and bait catches per hour of soak, and tallies your catch record card.

27
00:01:59,250 --> 00:02:04,000
Clamming trips list the daylight minus tides for the next two weeks, with the right gear list and safety links.

28
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:08,250
Keep your real lures in a tackle box and pick them with one tap when you log a catch.

29
00:02:08,250 --> 00:02:12,250
Set daily limits. The app counts what you keep and warns you before you go over.

30
00:02:12,250 --> 00:02:16,750
Your log stays on your phone, and automatic backups keep a copy safe.

31
00:02:16,750 --> 00:02:21,000
Fishing before dawn? Night mode turns the screen dim red to protect your night vision.

32
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:26,500
Open the link in Safari or Chrome, then add it to your home screen.

